NiArkImporterExtraData,tail-length,"JS: fixed 38B raw tail after int+version-string","Physical: 41B tail (13B header + 7xf32 bbox+pad) — closure-confirmed 2343/2343 in slice; witness 457485.nif: bytes 39-41 of pad land as ArkTexture's ""3 unknown zero bytes""","HIST schema stub: UnknownBytes[13] + UnknownFloats[7] = 41B — matches physical; the JS 38+3 split = re-attribution of the importer pad bytes",PARSER_MISATTRIBUTION_BIT_COMPATIBLE,0,0,"Re-attribute the 3 bytes to the importer tail (semantic labels only; byte stream identical)",YES_MINOR
NiArkTextureExtraData,3-header-bytes,"JS: reads 3 unknown zero bytes BEFORE the name","Physical: those 3 bytes are the last 3 bytes of the PREVIOUS NiArkImporterExtraData 41B tail (bbox pad); ArkTexture itself starts directly with its Name","Baseline (NiExtraData v10): Name first — no header bytes",PARSER_MISATTRIBUTION_BIT_COMPATIBLE,0,0,"Drop the 3-byte pre-read; fix importer tail to 41B",YES_MINOR (same change as above)
NiArkTextureExtraData,entry-count-formula,"JS/R61: entryCount = (field2 >>> 8) & 0xFFFFFF; no fallback","Physical: field2>>8 == true count in 2319/2343 slice blocks (99.0%); 24 blocks deviate (17x count=1 with field2=0; 7x count=3 with field2>>8 in {1,2}); closure-accepted count is the byte truth; the 24 blocks carry f1=15 (24x)/f1=0x1000000 (3x) anomalous entries","No baseline (MindArk custom block; HIST stub reads NumTextures directly = wrong for v10)",PARSER_FIELD_WRONG_ON_24_BLOCKS,24 (slice; corpus-wide possibly more outside slice),24,"Add count-resolution fallback (try field2>>8, then numfield, then field1 — pick by next-block validation, like this run's closure search); investigate the f1=15 variant family",YES
